@* The solution-notes dialog (spec §6.2.4): a status control (_StatusControl) setting a task Done asks here how it was resolved.
   Rendered once by the layout. site.js fills in the task and any notes kept from an earlier close, and on Mark Done copies the
   notes into the control's form and posts it; Cancel puts the control back. The server refuses Done without notes regardless. *@
<div class="modal fade" id="solution-notes-dialog" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="solution-notes-title" aria-hidden="true" data-bs-backdrop="static">
    <div class="modal-dialog">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">
                <h2 class="modal-title h5" id="solution-notes-title">Mark Done</h2>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Cancel"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <p class="fw-semibold mb-2 js-solution-task"></p>
                <label class="form-label" for="solution-notes-text">Solution notes <span class="text-muted">(required)</span></label>
                <textarea class="form-control js-solution-text" id="solution-notes-text" rows="5" aria-describedby="solution-notes-help"></textarea>
                <div class="invalid-feedback">Say how the task was resolved.</div>
                <div class="form-text" id="solution-notes-help">How the task was resolved: what was done, the fix, the outcome. Use a comment for discussion.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Cancel</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-success js-solution-confirm">Mark Done</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
